---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const canonicalURL = `${SITE.url}${Astro.url.pathname}`;
---

<BaseLayout title="About" canonicalURL={canonicalURL}>
  <h1 style="font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 32px; margin-top: 0;">
    About
  </h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I write to understand things, not to explain things I already understand.
      Most posts start from a question I couldn't answer cleanly — and work through
      it in public, without pretending to have arrived at a final answer.
    </p>
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      Rob's Blog is built around two ideas: first principles and critical thinking.
      First principles means stripping a problem down to what you actually know,
      rather than inheriting someone else's framing. Critical thinking means
      treating your own conclusions with the same skepticism you'd apply to anyone else's.
    </p>
    <h2>The format</h2>
    <p>
      Posts are Q&A-driven. Instead of essay prose, I break each piece into the
      questions that actually structure the thinking — the ones worth asking before
      reaching for an answer.
    </p>
    <h2>Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      Roberto Reale. Curious about how things work, why people believe what they
      believe, and whether any of it holds up when you push on it.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
